<article class="env-lemma" id="07Y7">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07Y7">Lemma <span data-tag="07Y7">98.21.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : \mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{Y}$ be a $1$-morphism of categories fibred in groupoids over $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}$. Let </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ B' \ar[r] &  B \\  A' \ar[u] \ar[r] &  A \ar[u] }  \]
</div>
  <p> be a commutative diagram of $S$-algebras. Let $x$ be an object of $\mathcal{X}$ over $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$, let $y$ be an object of $\mathcal{Y}$ over $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(B)$, and let $\phi : f(x)|_{\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(B)} \to y$ be a morphism of $\mathcal{Y}$ over $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(B)$. Then there is a canonical functor </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \textit{Lift}(x, A') \longrightarrow \textit{Lift}(y, B')  \]
</div>
  <p> of categories of lifts induced by $f$ and $\phi $. The construction is compatible with compositions of $1$-morphisms of categories fibred in groupoids in an obvious manner. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This lemma proves itself. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>